\title{Trait methods called with the dot on a vector}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-15}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{language}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1037}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|a.add(b)~} and \code{\verb~|x.neg()~} are accepted on a \code{\verb~|Simd~} vector and mean the same as \code{\verb~|a + b~} and \code{\verb~|-x~}. Before, the dot form was rejected with a field access error while \code{\verb~|Add::add(a, b)~} was accepted. See [ins-YAS4](ins-YAS4). \pr{1037}.}
